  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c9f2e8e5b57bd4bd99f33dd56077c2d1, type: 3}
  m_Name: KB_037_FirewallBlocking
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: POSTechSupport::POSTechSupport.Data.KnowledgeArticleSO
  articleId: KB-037
  title: Cards fail while the internet is fine
  category: 4
  content: "Two different faults produce this and neither is 'the internet is down'.
    A firewall blocks one outbound port and leaves everything else working; a wrong
    system clock (KB-016) fails the secure handshake with everything else working.
    Both let the customer browse the news while cards decline.\nCheck the clock first
    \u2014 it takes a second and rules out half the problem. If the clock is right,
    look at what is filtering outbound traffic to the processor."
  relatedErrorCodes: []
  guidanceForIssueIds:
  - P37
